<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>group.com.onlytrusted.app.shared</string>
    </array>
    <!--
      Family Controls (Phase 2 — App Shield / Selected Apps Restriction).

      This entitlement is NOT auto-provisioned by Apple. Apple reviews each app
      individually and only grants it to apps that pass a manual review as a
      "family safety / parental control" tool. For OnlyTrusted the request has to
      be filed via https://developer.apple.com/contact/request/family-controls-distribution/
      BEFORE the first App Store submission that uses the entitlement.

      The iOS Simulator does NOT fully support FamilyControls:
        * `AuthorizationCenter.shared.requestAuthorization(for: .individual)` throws.
        * `FamilyActivityPicker` renders but the returned tokens cannot be applied.
      AppShieldManager detects the simulator and shows an honest "requires device +
      Apple-approved entitlement" message instead of crashing.

      Until Apple approves the request on the real team ID, device builds that keep
      this key will fail code-signing with "Provisioning profile doesn't include
      the com.apple.developer.family-controls entitlement". That is expected and is
      the signal to remove the key temporarily or to finish the Apple request.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.developer.family-controls</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
